#! Completion, pinned by a transcript for the FIRST TIME (le07), and it
#! does not offer `byte`.
#!
#! docs/MATRIX.md has carried "completion | served (s122) | evidence:
#! transcripts/requests/*" since s133. Measured at le07: no transcript in
#! this library had ever sent `textDocument/completion` — the word only
#! ever appeared inside `initialize` capability blocks. The row claimed
#! evidence it did not have, which is the one failure that file exists to
#! prevent. This script is that evidence, and it records what the server
#! ACTUALLY answers rather than what the row implied.
#!
#! The le07 contract asked for "a completion transcript including
#! `byte`". The server does not offer it, so this transcript pins the
#! absence exhaustively instead of inventing the presence:
#!
#!   15:16  inside `List[byte]`'s type argument — TYPE position, the one
#!          place a type name is the only legal completion. The answer is
#!          the locals in scope, the file's functions, and all FIFTY
#!          reserved keywords ([gram.inv.kw]'s closed set, checksum 50) —
#!          and not one of the sixteen builtin type names. Not `byte`,
#!          not `int`, not `str`, not `bool`. A user typing a type
#!          annotation in any editor is offered `while` and `spawn`, and
#!          never the type they are annotating with. The item list is
#!          recorded whole, so the day builtins are added this record
#!          moves. Filed upstream.
#!
#!   25:15 after `.` — the trigger character the server ADVERTISES in its
#!          own `completionProvider.triggerCharacters: ["."]`. It answers
#!          an EMPTY list: member completion is not served, while the
#!          capability tells every client to fire a request on every dot.
#!          A second finding, filed with the first.
#!
#! Both records are regression witnesses pointed the right way: they are
#! red-flag shapes, committed so that fixing them is visible as a diff
#! rather than silently absent.
name      requests/completion-byte
profile   minimal

initialize
open      strings/bytes_roundtrip.lu
wait      diagnostics strings/bytes_roundtrip.lu
req       completion strings/bytes_roundtrip.lu 15:16
req       completion strings/bytes_roundtrip.lu 25:15 .
shutdown
